From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: S905L3 local bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: amlogic: m302a: use conservative eMMC timing

The S905L3/X96 Mini board boots from microSD, while the internal eMMC is on
the sd_emmc_c controller. The stock M302A node enables 8-bit high-speed, DDR,
and HS200 modes at up to 200 MHz, but this board fails tuning and never
creates the eMMC block device with that configuration.

Use the known-good fallback profile previously verified on this board: 1-bit
legacy timing capped at 20 MHz, with requests limited to 8 blocks so early
mmcblk probing cannot issue larger transfers that fail on this board. This
keeps Linux enumerating the internal eMMC for read-only inspection while
keeping the microSD rootfs on sd_emmc_b.

Signed-off-by: S905L3 local bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905l3b-m302a.dts | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905l3b-m302a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905l3b-m302a.dts
index f4a939a34..70e020338 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905l3b-m302a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905l3b-m302a.dts
@@ -47,11 +47,12 @@ &hdmi_tx {
 
 &sd_emmc_c {
 	status = "okay";
-	bus-width = <8>;
-	cap-mmc-highspeed;
-	mmc-ddr-1_8v;
-	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
-	max-frequency = <200000000>;
+	/delete-property/ cap-mmc-highspeed;
+	/delete-property/ mmc-ddr-1_8v;
+	/delete-property/ mmc-hs200-1_8v;
+	bus-width = <1>;
+	amlogic,max-request-blocks = <8>;
+	max-frequency = <20000000>;
 };
 
 &internal_phy {
